5755
05:00:02,650 --> 05:00:04,290
And there's some new advancements and stuff.

5756
05:00:04,450 --> 05:00:05,690
Other than that, I don't really know anything.

5757
05:00:07,030 --> 05:00:08,490
And I think it's best to keep it that way.

5758
05:00:09,910 --> 05:00:11,290
It's always nice to be surprised.

5759
05:00:14,690 --> 05:00:16,350
Dark oak with birch is nice.

5760
05:00:17,250 --> 05:00:19,830
Yeah, I can imagine the contrast there would be cool.

5761
05:00:24,130 --> 05:00:27,350
Are you planning to experiment with more building materials this season?

5762
05:00:27,450 --> 05:00:31,330
I'm just gonna play, and maybe if it makes sense at the time, I'll do it.

5763
05:00:32,330 --> 05:00:33,830
But here's the thing, it's really simple.

5764
05:00:33,890 --> 05:00:35,590
I'm just gonna sit down and play Minecraft.

5765
05:00:36,550 --> 05:00:38,830
And if it makes sense at the time, I'll try it.

5766
05:00:39,470 --> 05:00:42,470
I don't have any, like, ultra-specific goals like that in mind.

5767
05:00:42,530 --> 05:00:44,890
Other than, you know, try and get as many advancements as I can.

5768
05:00:45,490 --> 05:00:45,990
You know?

5769
05:00:47,770 --> 05:00:50,650
Anything else is just gonna be natural, stemming from that.

5770
05:01:00,100 --> 05:01:01,200
VideoBusters, I don't know yet.

5771
05:01:02,140 --> 05:01:04,560
I'll probably just wait, so nothing breaks.

5772
05:01:07,730 --> 05:01:09,210
Oliver, do you have Minecraft skin?

5773
05:01:09,270 --> 05:01:10,390
I don't think... I don't think so.

5774
05:01:12,810 --> 05:01:15,070
What are your top five games since starting the channel?

5775
05:01:15,170 --> 05:01:16,150
You mean the games I've played?

5776
05:01:17,810 --> 05:01:18,230
Uh...

5777
05:01:18,230 --> 05:01:19,890
Well, it's gotta be Outer Wilds.

5778
05:01:21,910 --> 05:01:23,670
That's my number one on the channel.

5779
05:01:23,850 --> 05:01:26,210
And it's not just because it's the most popular among the viewers.

5780
05:01:26,210 --> 05:01:28,830
It's legitimately also just a super good game.

5781
05:01:35,270 --> 05:01:35,690
Uh...

5782
05:01:35,690 --> 05:01:38,670
Why do I have trouble deciding now?

5783
05:01:39,790 --> 05:01:42,830
When I get put on the spot like that, I can't remember what the fuck I've played.

5784
05:01:46,160 --> 05:01:47,260
Wait a minute, let me see here.

5785
05:01:48,580 --> 05:01:49,640
What else did I play?

5786
05:01:54,670 --> 05:01:56,510
Rain World was amazing.

5787
05:01:57,670 --> 05:01:59,950
I mean, there's so many good ones, holy shit.

5788
05:01:59,990 --> 05:02:01,950
I've played so many games on the channel.

5789
05:02:03,050 --> 05:02:04,870
But I can tell you, before the channel...

5790
05:02:06,290 --> 05:02:07,350
Single-player games?

5791
05:02:07,770 --> 05:02:09,190
The Last of Us 1 and 2.

5792
05:02:09,330 --> 05:02:10,310
Holy crap!

5793
05:02:11,270 --> 05:02:12,870
Those two games...

5794
05:02:12,870 --> 05:02:15,110
Make me cry like a little bitch.

5795
05:02:16,290 --> 05:02:17,590
Because they're so good.

5796
05:02:17,870 --> 05:02:21,330
Just hearing the music swells me up with emotion.

5797
05:02:22,110 --> 05:02:26,790
And the second one specifically is so well done in every single fucking way.

5798
05:02:26,930 --> 05:02:27,770
It's insane.

5799
05:02:29,050 --> 05:02:32,650
I'm kinda sad I didn't play that until after I started the channel.

5800
05:02:32,930 --> 05:02:33,350
But yeah.

5801
05:02:34,490 --> 05:02:35,990
I loved Subnautica.

5802
05:02:37,410 --> 05:02:39,490
Bloodborne was unbelievably good.

5803
05:02:42,290 --> 05:02:43,290
Uh, what else?

5804
05:02:43,830 --> 05:02:46,070
The Talos Principle, holy crap.

5805
05:02:46,530 --> 05:02:48,030
Can't wait to play the second one.

5806
05:02:49,850 --> 05:02:51,210
I've played mostly Bangers.

5807
05:02:52,710 --> 05:02:56,450
I think my least favorite game has gotta be, uh...

5808
05:02:56,450 --> 05:02:57,270
Terraria, probably.

5809
05:02:58,990 --> 05:02:59,990
Breath of the Wild.

5810
05:03:00,130 --> 05:03:02,790
I wouldn't say it's in the same class as the other games I just mentioned.

5811
05:03:02,910 --> 05:03:03,450
But it's still good.

5812
05:03:03,750 --> 05:03:04,910
It was a great experience.

5813
05:03:05,610 --> 05:03:08,530
But it's not like mind-blowingly good as some of the others here.

5814
05:03:08,530 --> 05:03:10,050
It was a good game, for sure.

5815
05:03:11,310 --> 05:03:15,110
Breath of the Wild was such a good time to play whenever I came home from work.

5816
05:03:15,650 --> 05:03:16,150
You know?

5817
05:03:16,270 --> 05:03:18,370
Just to sit down and relax with a nice game.

5818
05:03:19,670 --> 05:03:20,790
Breath of the Wild, man.

5819
05:03:21,130 --> 05:03:22,350
It was the perfect game for that.

5820
05:03:23,950 --> 05:03:25,490
I have not played Tears of the Kingdom.

5821
05:03:31,140 --> 05:03:32,520
It is a cozy game, Mike.

5822
05:03:36,020 --> 05:03:38,260
I feel like you'd love Valheim a lot when it's complete.

5823
05:03:38,400 --> 05:03:39,200
So here's the thing, Isanti.

5824
05:03:39,600 --> 05:03:42,380
I played an hour with it with my friend, Peter.

5825
05:03:43,420 --> 05:03:45,080
Maybe, like, two years ago.

5826
05:03:45,460 --> 05:03:46,980
Actually, I don't remember exactly when it was.

5827
05:03:47,500 --> 05:03:49,840
But we decided then and there, okay, this shit is good.

5828
05:03:49,940 --> 05:03:51,660
We're gonna wait until it releases fully.

5829
05:03:51,920 --> 05:03:54,320
So I haven't touched it since, hoping that it'll release one day.

